The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (p4d_none(*p4d)) {
    pud = vmem_crst_alloc(_REGION3_ENTRY_EMPTY);
    if (!pud)
        goto out;
}
```
Reason:
The newly allocated page upper directory (PUD) entry (`pud`) is not linked to the page four directory (P4D) entry (`p4d`). This missing linkage causes the memory management system to fail when trying to access the PUD entry, leading to kernel crashes when 4-level paging is used.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
p4d_populate(&init_mm, p4d, pud);
```
Reason:
The `p4d_populate` function properly links the newly allocated PUD entry to the P4D entry, ensuring that the memory management system can correctly access the PUD entry. This linkage prevents the kernel crashes associated with the improper handling of 4-level paging.

